  "term": "consonant",
  "definition": "In this context, consonant refers to a type of sound or chord that listeners judge as pleasant in contrast to dissonant sounds, which are judged as unpleasant. The packet supports this meaning specifically for isolated piano-timbre chords used in affective neuroscience research.",
